# Answer key for the "energy-utility" gold dataset (Postgres) — HUMAN-MAINTAINED.
# One JSON object per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # or // are ignored.
# Wave B1.b of Milestone 1.23 (F1.23.4): statistical-power wave — fixtures sized so every
# dimension's pooled Wilson 95% lower bound clears 0.80 instead of resting on n=1 rows.
# Story: regional electricity utility two years after a big-bang CIS cutover — FKs re-added
# NOT VALID, AMI files landing in constraint-free staging tables, one fan-out reporting view.
# See ./README.md for the planted-defect table.
#
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"premises","field":"postal_code","severity":"low","note":"planted: postal_code is null on 4.1% (34000/820000) of premises — the address-cleansing job stopped writing it after the cutover, so meter-reader routing falls back to free text."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"meter","entity":"premises","field":"region_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: region_cd stored as NORTH / north / North / \"SOUTH \" ... — 34 raw values collapse to 28 normalized."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"premises","field":"geo_zone","severity":"medium","note":"planted: geo_zone is null on 12.9% (106000/820000) of premises — the GIS enrichment feed only covers the districts migrated in phase 1."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"meter","entity":"premises","field":"connection_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: connection_date has a 2087-12-31 sentinel used by the legacy CIS for \"not yet energised\" — a future date in a column that records when supply actually started."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"meter","entity":"premises","field":"mpan","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 140 duplicate MPANs (the metering point reference that must be unique nationally) — the CIS migration re-issued MPANs for two converted districts."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"meter","entity":"meters","field":"device_uuid","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 640 device_uuid values are not UUIDs (the head-end wrote the legacy 12-char device code instead) — they fail the uuid format."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"meters","field":"firmware_version","severity":"medium","note":"planted: firmware_version is null on 22% (272800/1240000) of meters — the OTA inventory sync only reports meters that checked in since the platform migration, so patch compliance cannot be computed for the rest."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"meter","entity":"meters","field":"serial_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 1240 duplicate meter serial numbers on the declared UNIQUE key — a converted district was loaded twice during the cutover weekend and the de-dup step was skipped."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"meter","entity":"meter_reads","field":"consumption_kwh","severity":"low","note":"planted: consumption_kwh reaches -4200 — reversed current transformers on a block of industrial sites report negative consumption, which corrupts every downstream settlement aggregate."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"meter_reads","field":"quality_flag","severity":"low","note":"planted: quality_flag is null on 8.2% (33600000/410000000) of reads — the validation stage skips rows that time out, so their estimated/actual status is unknown."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"read_batches","field":"operator_name","severity":"medium","note":"planted: operator_name is null on 15% (12900/86000) of batches — automated head-end pulls do not stamp an operator, so batch provenance is lost for exactly the loads nobody reviewed."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"install_jobs","field":"technician_id","severity":"low","note":"planted: technician_id is null on 9% (8460/94000) of jobs — third-party contractor crews are booked without a technician record, so no install can be traced to a person."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"meter","entity":"install_jobs","field":"duration_minutes","severity":"low","note":"planted: duration_minutes reaches -45 — handheld clocks drift and jobs closed before their recorded start produce negative durations, which skew every crew-productivity report."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"meter","entity":"install_jobs","field":"start_at, end_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: the whole end_at range (2018-11-02 … 2025-12-30) precedes the whole start_at range (2019-03-01 … 2026-08-04) — the two columns were mapped the wrong way round in the work-order migration."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"meter","entity":"firmware_versions","field":"release_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 18 release_url values are bare host names copied from the vendor portal without a scheme — they fail the url format and break the firmware-notes link in the UI."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"firmware_versions","field":"certified_by","severity":"medium","note":"planted: certified_by is null on 30% (72/240) of firmware versions — pre-2021 releases were certified on paper, so the regulator-facing report has gaps."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"meter_events_archive","field":"event_code","severity":"low","note":"planted: event_code is null on 4% (480000/12000000) of archived events — the legacy exporter dropped codes it could not map, so those events are untriageable."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"meter","entity":"meter_events_archive","field":"event_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: event_at reaches back to 1899-12-30 — the spreadsheet epoch, written whenever the legacy exporter met an empty timestamp. Those rows are not 19th-century events, they are nulls in disguise."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"meter","entity":"meter_events_archive","field":"event_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest event_at is 2024-03-18 (877 days stale) — event archiving was pointed at the new platform in early 2024 but this table was never decommissioned, so dashboards still joining it silently read frozen data."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"meter","entity":"v_meter_state","field":"meter_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the view is specified as one row per meter, but a join against the multi-row firmware history fans out and leaves 3100 duplicate meter_id values — consumers that count rows over-report the fleet."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"meter","entity":"v_meter_state","field":"estimation_pct","severity":"medium","note":"planted: estimation_pct maxes at 118.4 in a column named as a percentage — estimated reads are divided by a stale denominator, so the share of estimated consumption exceeds 100%."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"meter","entity":"v_meter_state","field":"last_read_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: last_read_at is null for 5% (62000/1240000) of meters — meters that have never reported since the cutover, indistinguishable in the view from meters read today."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"meter","entity":"stg_ami_reads","field":"read_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 412000 duplicate read_id values in the landing table — the head-end re-delivers a file whenever an acknowledgement is missed, and nothing de-duplicates before the merge."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"meter","entity":"stg_ami_reads","field":"register_value","severity":"low","note":"planted: register_value uses -9999 as the head-end's \"no read\" sentinel — a negative in a cumulative register column, which any aggregation reads as a real meter rollback."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"meter","entity":"stg_ami_reads","field":"read_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 84000 read_date values arrive as DD/MM/YYYY from one head-end region instead of ISO — they fail the date-string format and parse as null downstream."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"meter","entity":"stg_meter_master","field":"meter_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 2400 duplicate meter_id values in the master landing table — two regional extracts overlap on the districts transferred mid-year."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"meter","entity":"stg_meter_master","field":"install_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 3100 install_date values are the string \"UNKNOWN\" written by the extract when the source field is empty — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"billing","entity":"accounts","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: contact_email is null on 11% (86900/790000) of accounts — paperless-billing enrolment was never backfilled for accounts migrated in phase 1, so those customers cannot be notified electronically."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"billing","entity":"accounts","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 3800 contact_email values are malformed (missing @ or domain) — branch staff typed them into a free-text field with no validation."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"billing","entity":"accounts","field":"mobile_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 1200 mobile_number values still carry the legacy CIS internal codes (\"N/A\", \"SEE NOTES\") — they fail the phone format, so outage SMS silently drops them."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"billing","entity":"accounts","field":"segment_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: segment_cd stored as RESI / resi / Resi / SME / sme ... — 19 raw values collapse to 12 normalized, so segment revenue splits double-count."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"billing","entity":"accounts","field":"billing_address","severity":"low","note":"planted: billing_address is null on 6% (47400/790000) of accounts — the migration only carried the address when it differed from the premise, but the \"same as premise\" flag was dropped, so paper bills bounce."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"billing","entity":"accounts","field":"account_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 310 duplicate account_no values on the declared UNIQUE key — the CIS migration re-used account numbers freed by closed accounts."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"billing","entity":"invoices","field":"due_date","severity":"low","note":"planted: due_date is null on 3% (840000/28000000) of invoices — the term-calculation step fails when the tariff has no payment terms, and dunning skips every invoice it cannot date."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"billing","entity":"invoices","field":"invoice_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 2400 duplicate invoice_no values on the declared UNIQUE key — the parallel-run period issued the same invoice number from both the legacy and the new biller."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"billing","entity":"invoice_lines","field":"cost_center_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: cost_center_cd is null on 18% (16920000/94000000) of lines — network-charge lines are generated by a rule that predates cost-centre allocation, so regulated-revenue reporting is incomplete."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"billing","entity":"payments","field":"reference_no","severity":"low","note":"planted: reference_no is null on 7% (1820000/26000000) of payments — direct-debit collections carry no customer reference, so unmatched-cash investigations have nothing to search on."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"billing","entity":"tariffs","field":"regulator_ref","severity":"high","note":"planted: regulator_ref is null on 55% (770/1400) of tariffs — only tariffs filed after 2021 carry the regulator reference, so the price-cap compliance extract covers less than half the book."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"billing","entity":"stg_billing_export","field":"invoice_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 18400 duplicate invoice_id values in the export landing table — a re-run of the nightly export appended instead of replacing."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"billing","entity":"stg_billing_export","field":"bill_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 2400 bill_date values are empty strings written by the exporter when the invoice has no issue date — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"billing","entity":"stg_payment_file","field":"payment_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 9600 duplicate payment_id values in the bank-file landing table — the same settlement file is picked up twice whenever the SFTP poll overlaps the bank's retransmission window."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"billing","entity":"stg_payment_file","field":"value_dt","severity":"medium","note":"planted: value_dt carries a 2099-12-31 sentinel for \"value date pending\" — a future date in the column that drives cash allocation and interest calculation."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"billing","entity":"legacy_cis_customers","field":"customer_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 5400 duplicate customer_id values — the legacy CIS allowed the same customer number in two branches, which is exactly why the new platform re-keyed them."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"billing","entity":"legacy_cis_customers","field":"opened_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: opened_on reaches back to 1753-01-01 — the SQL Server minimum date, written by the original loader wherever the opening date was blank."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"billing","entity":"legacy_cis_customers","field":"updated_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest updated_at is 2023-11-20 (996 days stale) — the legacy CIS was switched off at the cutover, but the table stayed in the schema and three reports still read customer names from it."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"meter","entity":"meters","field":"premise_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 8400 meters point at a premise_id with no premises row — demolished/de-energised premises were purged while their meters stayed in the fleet."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"meter","entity":"meter_reads","field":"meter_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 96000 reads reference a meter that no longer exists — meters removed during the exchange programme were deleted rather than retired."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"meter","entity":"install_jobs","field":"meter_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 1800 install jobs reference a meter_id that was never created — jobs raised against a planned meter that the exchange programme cancelled."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"meter","entity":"meter_events_archive","field":"meter_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 240000 archived events reference meters deleted in the cutover — the archive was never re-pointed, so event history cannot be joined back to the fleet."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"billing","entity":"accounts","field":"premise_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 3200 accounts reference a premise that does not exist — cross-schema FK left NOT VALID after the premise purge."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"billing","entity":"invoices","field":"account_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 12400 invoices reference an account_id with no accounts row — accounts closed and purged under retention while their invoices stayed for tax."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"billing","entity":"invoice_lines","field":"invoice_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 88000 invoice lines have no parent invoice — the cancel-and-rebill routine deletes the header and leaves the lines."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"billing","entity":"payments","field":"account_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 4100 payments reference a purged account — cash that can no longer be attributed to a customer."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"billing","entity":"payments","field":"invoice_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 148000 payments carry an invoice_id that matches no invoice — the bank-file loader writes the customer's quoted reference straight into the column without checking it."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"billing","entity":"invoice_lines","field":"tariff_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 3900 invoice lines reference a tariff_id that was retired and deleted rather than end-dated."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"meter","entity":"install_jobs","field":"premise_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 2100 install jobs reference a premise that no longer exists — no FK was ever declared on this column, so nothing stopped it."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"meter","entity":"v_meter_state","field":"meter_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the state view carries 3100 meter_id values with no meters row — the view reads from the staging table, which still holds meters deleted from the fleet."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"billing","entity":"stg_billing_export","field":"invoice_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 24000 rows in the export landing table reference invoices that were cancelled and deleted between the extract and the load."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"meter","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on meter.field_audit_log (retained under a separate DPA) — 1 of 11 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"billing","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on billing.billing_secrets (payment credentials vault) — 1 of 9 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
